     {
      "id": "6ad0a2296e62ea0455487f25",
      "fieldData": {
       "acrm---key-feature-4-content": "<h3>Reminders for anyone who has not filed</h3><p>The form sends an email or Slack reminder to each person who has not filed by your due date. People who already filed hear nothing, and the list of names shrinks each day.</p>",
       "afb---how-to-step-5-des": "Say who gets a reminder after the due date and who approves a change, such as an HR coordinator. Name one person rather than a whole team."
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6afac9f880ba78ea4157da4b",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---how-to-step-2-des": "Write each goal so the employee can hit it and you can count it. Give it a unit, a target, and a deadline inside the plan window. A goal with any of those missing stays a draft. Nobody signs a plan that cannot be judged."
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adb1c3938ede0a6d1170179",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---integration-feature-1": "<h3>Knife 301 is spot 1 on the waitlist</h3><p>Tavish Forge hammers out one run of 300 chef's knives at $145 each, and the form says the run ships the week of Jan 11. Every order after 300 goes to the waitlist for the next run. Winnifred Mabe places order 301 and becomes spot 1.</p>",
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Pre-Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a pre order form?\", \"a\": \"A pre order form takes orders for an item before it is made or in stock. It records who ordered what, and when each order will be ready. The seller then makes or buys stock against those totals.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a pre-order form?\", \"a\": \"List your items, the most you can make of each, and the date each one is ready. Describe that in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it returns a working form that stops selling each item at its limit and takes no orders after the last day you set.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a pre order form template include?\", \"a\": \"A pre order form template should include the buyer's contact details, each item with its price and a quantity box, the ready or ship date, and pickup or shipping details. Add a limit per item and a closing date. If you also keep a pre order form PDF at the counter for walk-in buyers, enter those orders into the same list to keep the counts right.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a free pre order form for a small business?\", \"a\": \"To make a free pre order form, start on Emergent's free tier. The free tier covers building and publishing. Describe your items, prices, limits, and ready dates in one prompt. Forms built with Emergent have no response caps, and a busy launch week never closes the form early. A school or team collecting sizes before a season can build a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/uniform-order'>uniform order form</a> the same way.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a pre-order form stop taking orders when an item sells out?\", \"a\": \"Set a limit on each item, and the form closes that item once submitted orders reach it. Count units, not orders: a buyer who takes 3 uses 3 of the limit. Then choose what a late buyer sees, such as a sold-out label, a date for the next batch, or a waitlist.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I do when orders from a pre-order form cannot ship on the promised date?\", \"a\": \"Tell each buyer before the date passes and ask whether they will wait. For most goods a customer orders by mail, telephone, fax, or on the Internet, the FTC's mail order rule says a seller who can ship later must seek the customer's consent to the delay. A seller who cannot ship must promptly cancel the order and make a full refund.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I turn pre-order form orders into a production plan?\", \"a\": \"Add up what each item needs for each ready date, then work back from the earliest date to set what gets made each day. Every order sits in a database you own, and a dashboard on that table shows the daily list. Some pre-orders end in a visit, such as installing shelving a buyer ordered; schedule that visit on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/work-order'>work order form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do customers choose a pickup time on a pre-order form?\", \"a\": \"Buyers pick from a list of pickup slots, each with its own limit, and a full slot drops off the list. Size each slot by how many orders your counter can hand out in that time. Repeat the slot and the pickup address in the confirmation email.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a pre-order form close?\", \"a\": \"Close it early enough to buy supplies and make everything before the ready date. Work back from that date: production time, plus the lead time on supplies, plus a day of slack. Set two closing rules on pre order forms with a fixed run, the date and the limit, and stop at whichever comes first.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one pre-order form handle sizes and colors?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give each item a size and a color choice, and set the limit per variant when each one runs out on its own, such as 40 mediums and 20 larges. In a form built with Emergent, you add a size or a color later by prompting. For shirts ordered in a size grid, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/t-shirt-order'>t shirt order form</a> with a quantity per size is a closer fit.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ad850ad3e9b6d3dd7f3a754",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Registrar sign-off comes before IT sees the request</h3><p>Westbrook College's IT office runs every new project through one form. Admissions wants campus tour sign-ups to create applicant records. The form asks which systems the work touches, and the answer includes the student records system. Registrar Dana Ortiz signs off first, before IT's Thursday intake meeting.</p>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf4f362aa9d681a57a6aad",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---mockup-data": "<p id=\"\">window.awbMockup = { restaurantKitchens: \"I run the kitchen at Lumen Bistro. Build a purchase order form my chefs fill on a phone at close: pick the supplier, add lines with item, cases and price per case, and show the running total. When they submit, email the supplier a PDF of the order and save it to a table I can check each morning.\", schoolDistricts: \"I handle purchasing for Cedar Hills School District. Build one purchase order form for teachers. The budget code dropdown should show only the codes for the teacher's department. If the total is over $1,000, require a vendor quote upload before the form can be submitted, and keep anything without one as a draft.\", factoryBuyers: \"I buy raw materials for Kessler Fabrication. Build a purchase order form with our vendor list, line items and a ship-to dock. Give each order the next PO number, add the vendor's payment terms, and email the vendor a PDF with a link to confirm the ship date. Show the confirmed date in the orders table.\", supplierIntake: \"My company is Oakes Packaging, a box supplier for grocery chains. Build a form where business customers send us their purchase orders. Require their PO number, a ship-to address, and the number of cases for each box size. Post every new order to our #orders Slack channel with the PO number first.\" };</p>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adb1c3938ede0a6d1170173",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Reference Check Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a reference check form?\", \"a\": \"A reference check form is the fixed set of questions an employer asks the people a candidate names as references, with room to record each answer. Reference check forms keep every finalist measured on the same points, and the notes stay on file with the hiring decision.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a reference check form?\", \"a\": \"Describe the role and the questions you want asked to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form from that prompt, along with the database behind it and a summary page for the hiring manager. Change any question later by asking for the change in plain English.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of a reference check form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The University of Northern Iowa's HR office publishes a sample that opens with \\\"Describe how long you have known this candidate and in what capacity.\\\" Further down, it asks whether the reference would have any reservations about rehiring the candidate. Copy those questions into your own reference check form, PDF or online, and edit them to fit the role.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a reference check form template include?\", \"a\": \"Include the candidate's name and the role, the reference's name and title, and how the two worked together. Then add your job-related questions with a notes box and a 1-5 rating under each, the rehire question, and the caller's name and the date. Consent for a criminal or credit history search goes on a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/background-check'>background check form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free reference check form with no response limit?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a reference check form. The forms it builds have no response caps, whether 3 references answer or 300.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many references should a reference check form ask for?\", \"a\": \"Ask for 3, and ask that at least one be a former direct manager. With 3 sets of ratings on the same scale, an average per work area means something, and a single low score stands out against the other two.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you send a reference check form to a candidate?\", \"a\": \"Send it after the final interview and before any offer goes out. Asking for references on the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/job-application'>job application form</a> collects names for applicants you will never call. Waiting until the shortlist means each reference you contact is tied to a real decision.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a reference check form when a reference only confirms title and dates?\", \"a\": \"Log the title and dates they confirm, and ask the candidate for one more name. An article on SHRM's site says that \\\"HR or a department manager typically provides a limited reference, confirming the employee's position and job tenure.\\\" A former client, or a manager from an earlier job, can speak to the work itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should fill in the reference check form during the call?\", \"a\": \"The person making the call, whether that is the hiring manager or a recruiter who knows the role well enough to ask a follow-up. Typing notes during the call beats rebuilding them from memory afterward. One university's sample form tells the caller to include the position, date and names of the candidate, the reference, and the person completing the check.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a current employee answer a reference check form for a candidate?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when they have seen the candidate's work, and their answers go on the same form as everyone else's. If that employee also recommended the candidate for the opening, log the recommendation on the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/employee-referral'>employee referral form</a> and keep the reference call as its own step. Emergent can build both forms on the same database.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
